 686:Core/Src/main.c **** /**
 687:Core/Src/main.c ****  * Producer side (called from ADC ISR). Accumulates STREAM_BATCH_SAMPLES samples
 688:Core/Src/main.c ****  * and pushes them as one frame; drops the whole batch if the FIFO is full.
 689:Core/Src/main.c ****  *
 690:Core/Src/main.c ****  * seq is advanced only on a successful push, which is what lets the host tell
 691:Core/Src/main.c ****  * the two loss modes apart: a FIFO overflow here leaves seq contiguous but
 692:Core/Src/main.c ****  * slower than wall-clock, while bytes lost on the wire leave holes in seq.
 693:Core/Src/main.c ****  */
